watcher_restart_test.py: the eval watcher killed again and again while it follows a replay of the dry run 2 commits.

Input: teams/05-architecture/results/dryrun2-1234/commits.jsonl from TSAI's run record (#869): 9 commits, step 0 to
the final step 1,221, sha256 05a052c390e6f80b7303eacd3be9b284c9a6a430e38478be5880012f75a2e0e8.
Two watchers as on the eval slot: Tier A on every commit, Tier B on every 3rd (it owns 3 of the 9; 10 on the slot),
one GPU slot lock. A supervisor restarts a watcher after exit 75 or a death by signal, never after 0, 1 or 78.

Planned kills (each fires once):
  SIGKILL while the scorer runs:              Tier A step 0 and step 1,221
  SIGKILL after the scorer wrote its result:  Tier A step 672, Tier B step 350
  SIGTERM while the scorer runs:              Tier A step 350 (the watcher must exit 75)
  with ClickHouse, SIGKILL from a proxy right after the server ran load_jsonl.py's DELETE (Tier A step 195) or its
  INSERT into eval_mini (Tier A step 513, Tier B last commit), before the watcher saw the answer
Random kills: 12 SIGKILLs at seeded random times (seed 7), to either tier. Some land while a watcher is down between
restarts; the log says how many hit a live watcher.

Fake store and scorer: the commits replayed at 200x (the run's 5,039 s in 25 s), a fake run_lab_ckpt.py that takes
1 s (200 s of run time), reads the pointer first and writes its result last, as run_lab_ckpt.py does.
Real store and scorer (--real, Linux, torch 2.15.0+cpu, kronecker-embeddings d07cb543): tests/replay_trainer.py
trains Team 5's tiny MoE and saves it with Team 7's Checkpointer at the 9 recorded steps and reasons, at the recorded
times at 40x, while the watchers run the real run_lab_ckpt.py --scorer smoke (export with the probe-loss check, then
the score, about 1.1 s per commit). Scorer processes are found in /proc every 10 ms; the /proc monitor lists each
overlapping pair from both sides.

"Base" is eval_watcher.py of the rollback branch this change builds on (6b35225d), without this change.

| # | Watcher | Store and scorer | Kills | Where | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | base | fake | planned | macOS 15.1, Python 3.12.4 | FAIL: 2 overlaps (step 0, step 1,221), 4 extra scorer runs |
| 2 | this change | fake | planned | macOS | PASS: 0 overlaps, 0 extra runs, 4 results kept after a kill |
| 3 | this change | fake + restore after commit 4 | planned + 12 random (10 hit) | macOS | PASS: 1 commit superseded, 0 extra runs |
| 4 | this change | fake, ClickHouse 24.8 | planned + 3 load kills | macOS | PASS: 12 run_ids, each 1 eval_mini row and 1 ingest_manifest row |
| 5 | this change | fake + restore, ClickHouse 24.8 | planned + load + 12 random (10 hit) | macOS | PASS: 12 run_ids as in run 4, 1 superseded |
| 6 | this change | fake | planned | Linux (Docker, Python 3.11) | PASS: 0 overlaps, 0 extra runs |
| 7 | base | real | planned | Linux | FAIL: 2 overlaps (step 0, step 1,221), 5 extra scorer runs |
| 8 | this change | real | planned | Linux | PASS: 0 overlaps, 0 extra runs |
| 9 | this change | real | planned + 12 random (12 hit) | Linux | PASS: 0 overlaps, 0 extra runs |

Tests in the same state: test_eval_watcher.py 58 passed, 1 skipped (the Linux-only PR_SET_PDEATHSIG test) on macOS;
the whole harness_lab/tests folder 95 passed on Linux (with lm_eval 0.4.13, datasets 5.1.0, tokenizers 0.23.3).

Commands (python = the repo's environment; ClickHouse = a throwaway clickhouse-server:24.8-alpine with schema_v1.sql;
Linux = docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/repo:ro -w /repo <python 3.11 image with torch, safetensors, pyyaml, numpy,
kronecker-embeddings> python ...):
  1. python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/watcher_restart_test.py --random-kills 0 --watcher <base eval_watcher.py>
  2. python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/watcher_restart_test.py --random-kills 0
  3. python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/watcher_restart_test.py --random-kills 12 --seed 7 --restore-after 4
  4. python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/watcher_restart_test.py --random-kills 0 --clickhouse-url http://127.0.0.1:18123
  5. python teams/09-evaluation/harness_lab/watcher_restart_test.py --random-kills 12 --seed 7 --restore-after 4 --clickhouse-url http://127.0.0.1:18123
  6. (Linux) watcher_restart_test.py --random-kills 0
  7. (Linux) watcher_restart_test.py --real --speed 40 --random-kills 0 --watcher <base eval_watcher.py>
  8. (Linux) watcher_restart_test.py --real --speed 40 --random-kills 0
  9. (Linux) watcher_restart_test.py --real --speed 40 --random-kills 12 --seed 7
--commits defaults to the dry run 2 record.

